(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[11 1 "// The builtins module's functions (Python/bltinmodule.c; PY5e). This file holds the functions on the"] [12 1 "// built-in types and the abstract API; the iterator types (enumerate, zip, map, filter, reversed,"] [13 1 "// callable_iterator) are builtins_iter.go's, exec/eval/compile builtins_exec.go's, __import__"] [14 1 "// import.go's. What depends on the data model's special methods of classes (format, dir's __dir__,"] [15 1 "// isinstance's __instancecheck__ ...) uses PY5c's slots and lookups when they exist."] [35 18 "// PyObject_ASCII: repr's object as it is"] [156 1 "// exactArgs checks a builtin's call has n positional arguments and no keywords."] [209 2 "// builtin_print_impl's writes (queue 232): each argument's str, the separators and the end written one by one, so a"] [210 2 "// file object's write sees them as CPython's print gives them (click's tests count a stream's writes)"] [212 3 "// the standard streams encode each str with the stream's encoding and errors (queue 242: PYTHONIOENCODING, a lone"] [213 3 "// surrogate under surrogateescape), the pieces written in order into the one buffer"] [273 1 "// asciiEscape is ascii()'s escaping of a repr: every non-ASCII code point as \\x, \\u or \\U."] [315 1 "// minMax is min() and max() (min_max): the items of one iterable or of the arguments, by key, the"] [316 1 "// first extreme kept; default for an empty iterable."] [478 43 "// a lone surrogate kept (PY6c)"] [486 11 "// bytes and bytearray of one byte too (builtin_ord; PY6c)"] [500 18 "// a lone surrogate one code point (PY6c)"] [511 2 "// any int, not only a C ssize_t (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_math's msum takes bin of a 2000-bit int)"] [537 2 "// slot_nb_divmod's vectorcall_maybe: a __divmod__ or __rdivmod__ set to None is called (TypeError), queue 264"] [565 2 "// PyNumber_Power's ternary_op (PY7: the built-in did ints by int64 and an object only by its __pow__, never the"] [566 2 "// exponent's __rpow__ nor a big int)"] [620 1 "// attrName is getattr's, setattr's, hasattr's and delattr's name: a str, or a str subclass's instance as its str"] [621 1 "// value (queue 203: CPython takes any str; test_dict's test_instance_dict_getattr_str_subclass)."] [642 3 "// with a default: _PyObject_LookupAttr's lookup, a module's missing name answered without its message's work"] [643 3 "// (module_getattro's suppress: no __spec__.has_location, a Python property, called; queue 293)"] [680 3 "// a generator's StopIteration carries its return value (PY7: next() raised a bare StopIteration, the slot's"] [681 3 "// Next ending with nil)"] [700 1 "// sortObjects sorts items in place by key (nil: the items) and reverse, stably: the keys computed in"] [701 1 "// order, then PY5b's SortObjects (list.sort's)."] [754 1 "// noFrameGlobals is the globals of a call with no Python frame: the running __main__'s"] [755 1 "// (_PyEval_GetGlobalsFromRunningMain), else a new dict."] [766 1 "// frameLocals is locals() of a frame (PEP 667): a module's or class's namespace (its mapping when that is no dict;"] [767 1 "// frameNamespace), else a new dict of a function's bound fast locals, cells and free variables, then its extra locals (the proxy's"] [768 1 "// snapshot, _PyEval_GetFrameLocals: a write to it does not reach the frame)."] [771 27 "// a call with no Python frame (an interpreter's call, queue 230)"] [803 1 "// builtinDir is dir(): the scope's names, or an object's __dir__() sorted (PY5c's lookup); without a"] [804 1 "// __dir__, a module's namespace, a type's and its bases', an object's type's and its __dict__'s."] [827 3 "// the object's __dir__ (object's, type's, module's, a class's own: PY5c's), its result sorted"] [843 3 "// the scope's names: a mapping not a dict (exec's locals; queue 219) by its keys"] [848 4 "// PyMapping_Keys"] [901 2 "// the readline module imported and both streams the process's terminals (builtin_input's tty path over"] [902 2 "// PyOS_Readline, queue 289): the line by its editor, the prompt its own"] [971 1 "// roundFloat is float.__round__ (Objects/floatobject.c's double_round): to an int, ties to even, without"] [972 1 "// ndigits; else the correctly rounded value at ndigits decimal places (round-half-even on the exact decimal"] [973 1 "// value, as dtoa's mode 3), negative ndigits rounding to tens, hundreds ..."] [995 2 "// the exact decimal value of x, rounded half-even at n places after the point"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[20 48] [26 49] [40 47] [58 46] [64 48] [74 52] [89 41] [99 48] [108 41] [121 41] [137 52] [140 32] [146 51] [178 31] [211 31] [216 39] [224 28] [228 37] [237 37] [245 43] [249 35] [254 32] [265 35] [292 46] [296 22] [306 28] [309 43] [339 34] [359 44] [414 45] [437 43] [451 43] [465 46] [482 46] [490 43] [508 45] [516 23] [530 39] [538 48] [541 49] [547 37] [576 25] [592 20] [592 28] [604 32] [631 40] [634 43] [654 37] [657 40] [670 37] [673 40] [679 34] [748 44] [759 54] [773 28] [781 37] [784 40] [790 31] [806 36] [809 39] [819 24] [828 54] [836 44] [845 25] [859 29] [874 47] [875 27] [893 38] [896 41] [903 34] [928 44] [932 33] [941 32] [1005 30]]} (go/file "builtins.go" :imports [


